---
import Blurb from '../../Blurb.astro';
import TechChip from '../../TechChip.astro';
import './SpecialiseSection.css';

// Reason copy is written as multiline template literals for easier review/editing,
// then collapsed back into flowing single-line paragraph text for rendering.
const clean = (text: string) => text.replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim();

const languages = [
  {
    name: 'JavaScript/TypeScript',
    reason: clean(`
      An absolute weapon in the browser, JS is a critical tool to have in one's toolkit, from
      vanilla JS for simple but elegant solutions to react.js for sophisticated UI, JavaScript
      has the power to knock the user's socks off which is why I love it.
    `),
    frameworks: ['React', 'Next.js', 'Node.js', 'Astro'],
  },
  {
    name: 'Python',
    reason: clean(`
      From serverless firebase/AWS functions, API test scripts to working with data and
      AI, Python has proven itself time and time again to be a robust and flexible language
      allowing for untapped levels of creativity. It is one of my dearest.
    `),
    frameworks: ['Pandas', 'Firebase', 'OpenAI', 'Scikit-learn'],
  },
  {
    name: 'CSharp',
    reason: clean(`
      A heavy hitter in writing backend solutions, this strongly typed but succinct language brings sophisticated backend solutions to life, 
      and who doesn't love that!
    `),
    frameworks: ['Dotnet'],
  },
  {
    name: 'Dart',
    reason: clean(`
      A relative newcomer to my list, Dart (and Flutter) has made mobile app development the
      easiest it has ever been, it's purpose built and is exceptional for high performance animations,
      this is my go-to for new mobile apps.
    `),
    frameworks: ['Flutter'],
  },
];

const cloudAndData = [
  {
    name: 'AWS',
    reason: clean(`
      The cloud provider that needs no introduction. As pervasive as AWS is in the industry, it also
      has a lot going for it. For better or for worse, AWS is the main cloud provider I have used over my
      career, from building SEO performant solutions to ensuring that ordering systems are future-proof.
    `),
    frameworks: ['EC2', 'Lambda', 'S3', 'RDS', 'SQS'],
  },
  {
    name: 'Postgres',
    reason: clean(`
      Postgres has become the industry standard in recent years, I have always used it and am
      very familiar with the syntax, its robust data integrity, performance and extensibility
      make it a very difficult choice to ignore if you need a relational DB.
    `),
  },
  {
    name: 'Kubernetes',
    reason: clean(`
      Being no stranger to microservice architectures, a clear understanding of working with K8s
      is essential for distributed production workloads.
    `),
    frameworks: ['EKS', 'ECR'],
  },
  {
    name: 'MySQL',
    reason: clean(`
      Having powered more production web applications than almost any other database out there.
      Its speed, simplicity, and the sheer depth of tooling and hosting support around it make it a
      dependable default whenever a project calls for a straightforward, battle-tested relational store.
    `),
  },
];

const groups = [
  { id: 'languages', label: 'Languages', items: languages },
  { id: 'cloud', label: 'Cloud and Database tech', items: cloudAndData },
];
---

<Blurb id="craft" align="left" title="What I specialise in">
  <p>
    Here are the programming languages and technologies that I specialise in, these are the tools that have empowered
    me over the years to write code & infrastructure that makes a difference.
  </p>

  <div class="specialise-tabbed">
    <div class="specialise-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Specialisation categories">
      {groups.map((group, i) => (
        <button
          type="button"
          role="tab"
          class={`specialise-tab${i === 0 ? ' is-active' : ''}`}
          data-tab={group.id}
          aria-selected={i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'}
        >
          {group.label}
        </button>
      ))}
    </div>

    {groups.map((group, i) => (
      <div class="language-list specialise-panel" data-panel={group.id} hidden={i !== 0}>
        {group.items.map((item) => (
          <div class="language-item">
            <h3>{item.name}</h3>
            <p>{item.reason}</p>
            {item.frameworks && (
              <>
                <p class="frameworks-title">Specific frameworks</p>
                <div class="framework-list">
                  {item.frameworks.map((framework) => (
                    <TechChip label={framework} />
                  ))}
                </div>
              </>
            )}
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
</Blurb>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.specialise-tabbed').forEach((wrap) => {
    const tabs = wrap.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.specialise-tab');
    const panels = wrap.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.specialise-panel');

    tabs.forEach((tab) => {
      tab.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const target = tab.dataset.tab;

        tabs.forEach((t) => {
          const isActive = t === tab;
          t.classList.toggle('is-active', isActive);
          t.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(isActive));
        });

        panels.forEach((panel) => {
          panel.hidden = panel.dataset.panel !== target;
        });
      });
    });
  });
</script>
